#: ../../source/samples/pmp.md:8
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/samples/pmp.md:10
msgid ""
"A sample application demonstrating the usage of the TLK PMP API. It "
"protects the upper half of a 16-element array against all access, then "
"attempts to read or write the full array, triggering a PMP violation trap"
" on the protected region."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/samples/pmp.md:14
msgid "How It Works"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/samples/pmp.md:16
msgid "On startup the sample:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/samples/pmp.md:18
msgid ""
"*(Optional)* Configures PMP protection on `demo_array[8..15]` using the "
"selected address matching scheme. All permissions are disabled and the "
"entry is locked (`l = 1`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/samples/pmp.md:20
msgid ""
"*(Optional)* If `CONFIG_TLK_PMP_DEMO_SLEEP` is set, enters sleep for 500 "
"ms and wakes up, demonstrating that PMP state is correctly saved and "
"restored across the sleep."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/samples/pmp.md:22
msgid "Iterates over all 16 elements of `demo_array`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/samples/pmp.md:23
msgid "With `CONFIG_TLK_PMP_DEMO_READ` — reads and logs each value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/samples/pmp.md:24
msgid "With `CONFIG_TLK_PMP_DEMO_WRITE` — writes and logs each value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/samples/pmp.md:26
msgid ""
"Elements `[0..7]` complete successfully. On the first access to "
"`demo_array[8]` a PMP violation trap is raised."
msgstr ""

